WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:00.194 --> 00:01:01.127
[siren blares]

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:03.629
[music]

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:11.838
[Peter] Good morning, guys,
here in Flint, Michigan,

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:15.957
a place that I'd say nationwide
has a pretty tough reputation.

00:01:16.173 --> 00:01:20.733
But it's also the place that created
General Motors and a booming middle class

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:25.470
peaking at
about 200,000 people back in 1960.

00:01:25.537 --> 00:01:29.359
Since then
the population is less than half of that.

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:32.425
So what is it like here now in Flint?

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.292
What are the stories on the streets?

00:01:34.359 --> 00:01:35.820
Today, we're going to dive in

00:01:35.887 --> 00:01:39.342
and get a better look
of what this place is all about.

00:01:39.409 --> 00:01:40.534
Let's do this.

00:01:43.135 --> 00:01:44.738
Downtown Flint,

00:01:44.805 --> 00:01:49.142
gotta say this place immediately
has a feel of its own.

00:01:49.643 --> 00:01:52.358
Beautiful old bones here.
Look at this theater.

00:01:52.425 --> 00:01:53.778
The Capitol Theater.

00:01:54.245 --> 00:01:56.908
Looks like it's still happening here,
which is great.

00:01:56.975 --> 00:02:00.754
Just a testament to the times
when this place was thriving.

00:02:00.821 --> 00:02:04.183
It wasn't Detroit, it was Flint
for General Motors in the beginning.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:07.908
And so all these jobs came in here
and built up a city

00:02:08.513 --> 00:02:11.902
around basically one industry.

00:02:12.299 --> 00:02:15.269
But Flint, I gotta say, first impressions,

00:02:15.336 --> 00:02:17.903
you're seeing a hodgepodge
of things going on here.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:21.942
You see there's some energy
being put into this town.

00:02:22.009 --> 00:02:23.729
Look at this beauty.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:28.302
And guys, you're not going to believe
what I just pulled up on my phone.

00:02:28.369 --> 00:02:30.157
Right here, this very place,

00:02:30.224 --> 00:02:32.737
and maybe that's why the road's closed.

00:02:32.804 --> 00:02:34.337
Last night, a shooting.

00:02:35.016 --> 00:02:36.816
An actual murder down here.

00:02:37.309 --> 00:02:38.889
Someone was killed I believe.

00:02:38.956 --> 00:02:42.089
One dead, one hurt,
in Downtown Flint shooting.

00:02:42.156 --> 00:02:45.763
Saginaw and First,
which is this exact area.

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:48.301
So I was just about to say
how great it feels.

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:50.039
But it's a mixed bag.

00:02:50.798 --> 00:02:52.872
I'm sure as we'll get into all day today.

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:55.561
Hey, the shooting
was right here last night, huh?

00:02:55.628 --> 00:02:57.111
I think so. I don't know.

00:02:57.178 --> 00:02:59.352
I briefly saw it on the news.
I wasn't here.

00:02:59.419 --> 00:03:01.883
-Is it that bad downtown right now?
-I don't know.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.157
Normally, I've been downtown
plenty of times.

00:03:04.224 --> 00:03:06.723
It's like,
I don't ever really feel in danger.

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:09.902
But you know,
there's lots of criminals in Flint.

00:03:09.969 --> 00:03:13.410
So anything
could really happen theoretically.

00:03:14.005 --> 00:03:16.283
I don't ever feel like in danger.

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:18.105
-Stay away from shit like that.

00:03:18.172 --> 00:03:19.518
This city is f*cked.

00:03:19.585 --> 00:03:22.835
They may try to make it look ritzy
down here, but it's f*cked up.

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:23.735
-How so?

00:03:24.453 --> 00:03:26.319
-Because it's Flint f*cking Michigan.

00:03:26.386 --> 00:03:30.774
Because the politicians pocket money
and the police pocket money.

00:03:30.841 --> 00:03:32.813
And they don't fix the real problem.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:37.300
They don't go to the source of the problem
which is the rich motherf*ckers.

00:03:37.367 --> 00:03:38.793
They just don't give a f*ck.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:40.737
-You're not feeling Flint these days?

00:03:40.804 --> 00:03:43.905
No, I've lived here my whole life.
I was born at Hurley in '86.

00:03:43.972 --> 00:03:46.793
-Okay, was it worse
back in the day or is it worse now?

00:03:46.861 --> 00:03:48.611
-No, it's way worse now.
-Seriously?

00:03:48.678 --> 00:03:50.826
I could walk anywhere when I was a kid.

00:03:50.893 --> 00:03:52.265
-Now it's worse?
-Yeah.

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:53.710
-Okay. Take care, man.

00:03:53.777 --> 00:03:56.110
40 years old, you know. It's worse.

00:03:56.604 --> 00:03:58.702
So if you're new to my videos…

00:03:58.769 --> 00:04:01.917
You realize I like to
talk to as many people as possible.

00:04:01.984 --> 00:04:03.944
And so that's that man's opinion.

00:04:04.011 --> 00:04:05.914
We get as many opinions as we can.

00:04:05.981 --> 00:04:09.079
He could be 100% right.
I don't know. I'm not from here.

00:04:09.146 --> 00:04:12.203
But the style here
is to get it through the locals.

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:15.208
Not through a mouthpiece.
Not through a politician.

00:04:15.275 --> 00:04:17.416
But through what we come into.

00:04:18.125 --> 00:04:21.682
We can see J London's fine men's apparel.

00:04:21.749 --> 00:04:25.402
So you still got some of
these classic clothing shops.

00:04:25.469 --> 00:04:27.137
That's old school for sure.

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.506
Got some statues over here.

00:04:29.573 --> 00:04:31.877
A nice brick street.

00:04:31.944 --> 00:04:33.144
Henry Ford Health.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.474
University of Michigan Flint.

00:04:36.004 --> 00:04:38.120
Didn't expect to see that down here.

00:04:38.187 --> 00:04:41.681
Look, we got a Barnes and Noble downtown.
Fantastic.

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:44.339
And there's not much street life
so far today.

00:04:44.406 --> 00:04:45.406
It is a Sunday.

00:04:46.359 --> 00:04:49.474
So maybe the Flintstones sleep it in

00:04:50.021 --> 00:04:51.461
or just don't come downtown.

00:04:52.074 --> 00:04:53.327
-[siren blares]
-Not sure.

00:04:53.394 --> 00:04:55.127
Car coming pretty quickly.

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:57.262
[siren continues]

00:05:00.901 --> 00:05:02.901
[motorcycles pass]

00:05:06.173 --> 00:05:08.692
So we're just going to peel off
the main drag here.

00:05:08.759 --> 00:05:10.560
See if we can find some life.

00:05:11.926 --> 00:05:13.960
[woman] I was sitting in a cafe.

00:05:14.486 --> 00:05:16.675
I was sitting in that coffee house.

00:05:16.742 --> 00:05:19.149
And I'm like,
I know this guy from somewhere.

00:05:19.216 --> 00:05:21.788
-Are you a Flintstone?
-No, I'm from Saginaw.

00:05:21.855 --> 00:05:23.163
I watch you all the time.

00:05:23.236 --> 00:05:26.513
-Thank you. What's your name?
-Jennifer Marks.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:27.959
-Okay, I'm making a video on Flint.

00:05:28.026 --> 00:05:30.881
-What are you doing here?
-I come down here all the time.

00:05:30.947 --> 00:05:33.299
-Do you like it?
-Oh, yeah. I love it here.

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:36.619
My daughter dances in the Philorica dance

00:05:36.686 --> 00:05:39.005
at the Institute for Performing Arts.

00:05:39.072 --> 00:05:42.876
My sister and me used to work
down here in the Flint area.

00:05:42.943 --> 00:05:45.714
So we kind of just
always came down here to Flint.

00:05:45.781 --> 00:05:47.438
And just like the restaurants.

00:05:47.505 --> 00:05:50.172
Before it was…
They didn't have all this.

00:05:50.633 --> 00:05:52.315
-What do you mean the main drag?

00:05:52.388 --> 00:05:55.884
They didn't have all the businesses
like the Cork on Saginaw.

00:05:55.951 --> 00:05:58.824
And everybody just started
building businesses down here.

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:01.591
-Okay. So you're saying
it's going in a good direction.

00:06:01.658 --> 00:06:05.017
It's going in a good direction.
Kind of like Detroit is.

00:06:05.084 --> 00:06:06.884
-Detroit's nice now.
-Yeah.

00:06:06.951 --> 00:06:08.951
I'm surprised. That's where I'm staying.

00:06:09.018 --> 00:06:12.063
Downtown Detroit is nicer
than a lot of cities right now.

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:14.574
-Yeah. There's a renaissance.
-Clean, nice.

00:06:14.641 --> 00:06:18.580
Don't want to get dark,
but just gotta point the obvious.

00:06:18.647 --> 00:06:21.730
There was a murder last night.
Someone was shot and killed.

00:06:21.797 --> 00:06:24.366
So that stuff's happening.
There's still crime here.

00:06:24.433 --> 00:06:25.777
Yeah. There's still crime.

00:06:25.844 --> 00:06:28.071
-So you're not coming
and hanging out at nights?

00:06:28.138 --> 00:06:30.372
No, not in a crime area.

00:06:30.439 --> 00:06:33.101
Okay. So you come in during the day,
do your thing.

00:06:33.168 --> 00:06:35.943
-Your daughter comes, does her dancing.
-Yeah.

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:37.849
-And you go to a restaurant and go.

00:06:37.916 --> 00:06:38.749
-Yeah.
-Okay.

00:06:38.816 --> 00:06:40.283
I just come down here.

00:06:43.386 --> 00:06:46.526
As a video maker
I could show just that first guy

00:06:46.593 --> 00:06:50.489
and just look for those stories
or I could show just that woman

00:06:50.556 --> 00:06:52.156
and look for her stories

00:06:52.771 --> 00:06:55.647
and really nail down
on one side of things.

00:06:55.714 --> 00:06:57.267
But that's not my style.

00:06:57.334 --> 00:06:59.573
It's not what I want to see online.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:03.030
And that's why you're here most likely.
You don't want that either.

00:07:03.097 --> 00:07:07.227
Now what I run into is what I run into.
So that's the best I can give you.

00:07:08.553 --> 00:07:10.289
Here we have a Flint alleyway.

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:13.546
It's cool.
They're letting the art flourish.

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:16.203
Here's another one.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:20.301
That is awesome.
I've never seen that on power meters.

00:07:20.368 --> 00:07:22.561
Someone painting them up.
Looks really nice.

00:07:22.628 --> 00:07:25.103
Shout out to Angela Bower.
Love your style.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:26.237
That is so cool.

00:07:26.822 --> 00:07:28.720
Hey, they're trying here. I gotta say.

00:07:28.787 --> 00:07:31.454
They're definitely trying here in Flint.

00:07:32.953 --> 00:07:34.353
What do we have here?

00:07:34.997 --> 00:07:36.949
Local 432.

00:07:39.893 --> 00:07:41.524
What's going on here at 432?

00:07:41.591 --> 00:07:46.199
Right now we're doing a photo shoot
for John Hammon and his band.

00:07:46.266 --> 00:07:47.930
-Is that a local band?
-Yes it is.

00:07:47.997 --> 00:07:49.552
-Are they pretty good?
-Oh yeah.

00:07:49.619 --> 00:07:51.975
It's between rock and country.

00:07:52.042 --> 00:07:55.003
Kind of like a Bob Seger-ish
but a little bit more metal.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:58.378
-Are we going to drop in
a slide guitar occasionally?

00:07:58.445 --> 00:08:00.703
[chuckles] I don't know about tonight.

00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:02.796
-You're a large?
-I'm a large.

00:08:02.863 --> 00:08:05.585
-There you are, buddy.
-Thank you. I appreciate it.

00:08:05.652 --> 00:08:08.950
This is actually John Hammon right here.
This is his band.

00:08:09.017 --> 00:08:12.236
Okay. John Hammon Band.
I wish I had a third hand but I got you.

00:08:12.303 --> 00:08:13.551
All right.

00:08:13.618 --> 00:08:16.606
John Hammon
is like one side of the equation

00:08:16.673 --> 00:08:18.843
and Streetlight Saints is the band name.

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:22.326
-Okay. So what's your take
on the music scene in Flint right now?

00:08:22.393 --> 00:08:26.636
So people associate Flint
as being vehicle city.

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:28.362
-You know we're in GM town?
-Yeah.

00:08:28.429 --> 00:08:33.028
The truth of the matter is we have
more musicians than we have shop rats.

00:08:33.095 --> 00:08:34.463
This is a musical city.

00:08:35.062 --> 00:08:37.670
Anything that you want.
If you want rap, we got Dayton Family.

00:08:37.743 --> 00:08:41.096
If you want metal, we got Never The Crash.
We have Approaching Autumn.

00:08:41.163 --> 00:08:45.272
If you want bluegrass music, there's the
entire Michigan Bluegrass Association

00:08:45.339 --> 00:08:46.842
right here in Flint, Michigan.

00:08:46.909 --> 00:08:49.368
-So people are coming to see music here?

00:08:49.435 --> 00:08:52.385
Yeah. If they know about it,
people show up. It's beautiful.

00:08:52.452 --> 00:08:56.468
Isn't that usually the case when you have
a town that's gone through rough times?

00:08:56.535 --> 00:09:00.363
It gets cheaper and then the arts and
the creativity really start to flourish.

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:02.430
'Cause that's where the energy goes.

00:09:02.497 --> 00:09:03.963
I'll agree to that.

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:06.597
-Or where do I have that wrong?
-No, it's not wrong.

00:09:06.664 --> 00:09:09.296
I would say the music never stops.

00:09:09.363 --> 00:09:10.630
The art never dies.

00:09:11.149 --> 00:09:12.955
It just kind of goes through phases.

00:09:13.022 --> 00:09:16.769
As older generations move up,
the new ones come in.

00:09:16.836 --> 00:09:20.986
Which is one of the things
that we try to do. We elevate. We inspire.

00:09:21.053 --> 00:09:24.303
We try to write some new stuff
for everyone that wants to hear it.

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:28.253
I'll play a country song
but we're going to play some metal too.

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:31.570
-Oh, my wife will like you for that.
Slipknot's her favorite band.

00:09:31.637 --> 00:09:32.808
-I love Slipknot.
-Yeah.

00:09:32.875 --> 00:09:36.575
She's sweet and nice, but then she goes
to Slipknot and starts headbanging.

00:09:36.642 --> 00:09:39.292
-So it lets it out with the music, right?
-Yeah, dude.

00:09:39.359 --> 00:09:40.688
Music is a universal thing

00:09:40.755 --> 00:09:44.005
where it doesn't always happen
exactly the same every single show.

00:09:44.072 --> 00:09:45.822
Everything is unique in the moment.

00:09:45.889 --> 00:09:47.306
-Are you a Flintstone?
-I am.

00:09:47.373 --> 00:09:50.755
How would you say 2026 Flint,
you've been through some rough times.

00:09:50.822 --> 00:09:52.645
-Where is it at now?
-It's elevating.

00:09:52.712 --> 00:09:55.012
-And it's going up, you think?
-It's elevating.

00:09:55.079 --> 00:09:58.073
I think that we have a beautiful city that

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:01.223
every decade or so
kind of has a renaissance.

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:03.618
And right now,
there's a lot of people that are

00:10:03.685 --> 00:10:07.806
absolutely dedicated to doing
what they can to make our city beautiful.

00:10:07.873 --> 00:10:09.485
You see the murals.

00:10:09.552 --> 00:10:12.552
The arches were gone for 30 years
and they brought them back.

00:10:12.619 --> 00:10:16.563
-So local artists doing the murals?
-Yes. I don't know his name.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:19.431
-Oh, shout out to him whoever he is.
-Yeah.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.386
Many of you know me as a video maker,

00:10:27.453 --> 00:10:30.284
but for the first time
I can say I'm a published author,

00:10:30.351 --> 00:10:32.796
a New York Times bestselling author.

00:10:32.863 --> 00:10:37.022
Your fellow Americans, if you love
what you're seeing behind the screen,

00:10:37.089 --> 00:10:41.025
you're going to love the book 'cause
there's all sorts of stuff that's in here

00:10:41.092 --> 00:10:42.809
that you're not gonna see on YouTube.

00:10:42.876 --> 00:10:48.441
For example the time I was locked
out of my rental in Amish country

00:10:48.508 --> 00:10:51.674
in my underwear
and having to navigate that world.

00:10:51.741 --> 00:10:53.753
Which was quite challenging.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:56.928
Or just all the moments that happen when

00:10:57.428 --> 00:11:00.760
the power button's off
and getting deeper stories with people.

00:11:00.827 --> 00:11:03.300
Just a lot of
my favorite videos, actually.

00:11:03.367 --> 00:11:06.846
Some of the classics are in here,
but just with more history,

00:11:06.913 --> 00:11:08.870
more thoughts, more reflection,

00:11:08.937 --> 00:11:11.472
it's a deeper dive on the country.

00:11:11.539 --> 00:11:13.085
And then the last chapter,

00:11:13.152 --> 00:11:16.545
that's the one that's called
The Road Trip That Started It All.

00:11:16.612 --> 00:11:20.545
And that's my origin story
and how I got into this crazy lifestyle

00:11:20.612 --> 00:11:25.613
and wild career
of making videos across the country.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:27.920
All sorts of little nuggets in there.

00:11:27.987 --> 00:11:30.643
It's really a fun book.
I put a lot into it.

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:34.432
I think you're going to love it too.
Thank you all who've bought it so far.

00:11:34.499 --> 00:11:36.686
For those still looking to buy it,

00:11:36.753 --> 00:11:38.798
the quickest way is through Amazon.

00:11:38.865 --> 00:11:42.217
That link is somewhere around here
or down below in the description.

00:11:42.284 --> 00:11:45.389
If you want to support physical bookstores
like Barnes &amp; Noble,

00:11:45.456 --> 00:11:49.175
every Barnes &amp; Noble in the country
is carrying your fellow Americans,

00:11:49.242 --> 00:11:53.201
or indie bookstores,
many of them, not all, but many are.

00:11:53.268 --> 00:11:57.283
And if they don't have it, you can ask
and they'll order it for you.

00:11:57.350 --> 00:11:59.378
You're gonna love it. It's a great gift.

00:11:59.445 --> 00:12:01.616
It's a great coffee table book.

00:12:01.683 --> 00:12:02.733
It's a lot of fun.

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:06.351
It's our story of this beautiful country.

00:12:06.418 --> 00:12:08.064
Now back to the video.

00:12:11.901 --> 00:12:14.549
We got a big shout out to John Hammon.

00:12:14.616 --> 00:12:18.497
Didn't hear his music,
but just had that musician vibe to him

00:12:18.564 --> 00:12:20.266
where I bet he's really good.

00:12:20.816 --> 00:12:23.309
And he gave us our time.
So go check him out.

00:12:23.376 --> 00:12:25.395
Look at that. Keeps on going.

00:12:25.462 --> 00:12:26.896
How are you guys doing?

00:12:26.963 --> 00:12:28.471
-Are you guys from here?
-Yeah.

00:12:28.538 --> 00:12:30.249
-How's it going?
-Going good.

00:12:30.316 --> 00:12:31.883
-I like Flint.
-Yeah?

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:34.203
It's my favorite.
I grew up in Beecher though.

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:36.516
-That's like a district.
-Okay.

00:12:36.583 --> 00:12:38.883
We always competed against Flint schools.

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:40.877
Beecher schools is more suburb.

00:12:41.427 --> 00:12:42.726
-Is this apartments?

00:12:42.793 --> 00:12:45.775
These are lofts. There's only six units.

00:12:45.842 --> 00:12:49.335
-No way.
-Yeah. They like 2,300 square feet.

00:12:49.402 --> 00:12:53.124
The rent here is cheaper
than like big cities or wherever.

00:12:53.191 --> 00:12:55.058
-Cheaper than Detroit?
-Yeah.

00:12:55.611 --> 00:12:59.065
-Can you get a place for like a thousand?
-I would say Mich… No!

00:12:59.132 --> 00:13:01.751
I mean you wouldn't want it if it's…

00:13:01.818 --> 00:13:05.951
-So a good loft around here
is like $1,500, something like that?

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:07.260
More. Well…

00:13:08.154 --> 00:13:09.140
-Wow.

00:13:09.207 --> 00:13:12.984
Not cheap. All right.
Good luck, you guys. Take care.

